---
import Section from './Section.astro';
import { site } from '../consts';
---

<Section id="architecture" title="Architecture">
  <p>
    SSCCS is developed as a software-first system: a compiler toolchain, a runtime, and an open
    binary format, with the hardware architecture specified alongside them and derived from the same
    structure. The layers below are the ones that carry the model from a specification to a running
    substrate.
  </p>

  <dl class="defs">
    <dt>Lowering chain</dt>
    <dd>
      A structural description is compiled through a layered lowering chain onto hardware-specific
      backends. Each layer refines the description while the invariants of the model are preserved,
      and the structural document itself is what reaches execution, embedded rather than interpreted
      at run time.
    </dd>

    <dt>Hardware abstraction</dt>
    <dd>
      A target-agnostic hardware abstraction layer keeps the ontological core independent of the
      execution substrate. The same Scheme projects onto a CPU, an FPGA, or a processor-in-memory
      architecture without rewrites.
    </dd>

    <dt>Binary format</dt>
    <dd>
      The compiled artefact is an open binary format. The structural description and the executable
      are one document, so a deployment carries its own specification.
    </dd>

    <dt>Reference implementation</dt>
    <dd>
      A Rust reference implementation validates all core primitives under continuous integration.
      The same primitives are proven in parallel across RTL, RISC-V assembly, and current-language
      work in the <a href={site.poc}>proof-of-concept tree</a>, before the reference compiler and
      runtime take their final shape.
    </dd>
  </dl>
</Section>
